  "question": {
    "text": "<p>As shown in the figure, two parallel plate capacitors having equal plate area of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>200</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>cm</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math> are joined in such a way that <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi><mo>&#8800;</mo><mi>b</mi></math>. The equivalent capacitance of the combination is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><msub><mi>&#949;</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mi>F</mi></math>. The value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math> is _____.</p><p><img src=\"assets\\qt0041_4802a2967a88.png\" style=\"width: 400px; height: 242px;\" /></p>"
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "5",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>The given data is&nbsp;</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>200</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"></mspace><mi>d</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math></p><p>The value of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math></p><p>The formula for a parallel plate capacitor is&nbsp;</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>C</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>&#949;</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mi>A</mi></mrow><mi>D</mi></mfrac></math></p><p>Let the capacitor with gap&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi></math>&nbsp;be&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;and capacitor with gap&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>b</mi></math>&nbsp;be&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>&#949;</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mi>A</mi></mrow><mi>a</mi></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>&#949;</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mi>A</mi></mrow><mi>b</mi></mfrac></math></p><p>The equivalent capacitance is&nbsp;</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>e</mi><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>a</mi><mrow><msub><mi>&#949;</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mi>A</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mi>b</mi><mrow><msub><mi>&#949;</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mi>A</mi></mrow></mfrac><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"></mspace><mo>&#8658;</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>e</mi><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>&#949;</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mi>A</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></mfrac></math></p><p>It is given that&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>e</mi><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi><msub><mi>&#949;</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">F</mi></math></p><p>So,&nbsp;</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>&#949;</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mi>A</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi><msub><mi>&#949;</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"></mspace><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></mfrac><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"></mspace><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>200</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn></math></p></blockquote>"
  }
}